	Main.RealAPICatalog = {{n="cache.invalidate",c="Cache",s="cache.invalidate(instance: Instance)",d="Removes the cached Instance entry for the given Instance. It does not return data. Treat the call as an action and handle errors around the call site when needed. ### 📌 Example Remove an Instance from Real's cache and check whether the cache entry is still present."},{n="cache.iscached",c="Cache",s="cache.iscached(instance: Instance): boolean",d="Returns whether the given Instance has a non-nil entry in the Instance cache. It returns cached (boolean). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil results and recoverable errors. ### 📌 Example Check whether an Instance currently has an entry in Real's Instance cache."},{n="cache.replace",c="Cache",s="cache.replace(instance: Instance, replacement: Instance)",d="Sets the cached Instance entry for one Instance to another Instance. It does not return data. Treat the call as an action and handle errors around the call site when needed. ### 📌 Example Store one Instance as the cached entry for another Instance."},{n="cloneref",c="Cache",s="cloneref(instance: Instance): Instance",d="Pushes a new Instance reference for the same same underlying Instance and returns it. It returns reference (Instance). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil results and recoverable errors. ### 📌 Example Create another Instance reference from an existing Instance userdata."},{n="compareinstances",c="Cache",s="compareinstances(first: Instance, second: Instance): boolean",d="Compares the Instance references stored in two Instance object values. It returns equal (boolean). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil results and recoverable errors. ### 📌 Example Compare the underlying Instance references."},{n="base64_decode",c="Cryptography",s="base64_decode(data: string): string",d="Decodes Base64 input with Base64 decoder and returns the decoded bytes as a Lua string. It returns decoded (string). 