e when level < 0 or level >= the current call stack depth, otherwise true. "},{n="setconstant",c="Debug",s="setconstant(target: function | number, index: number, value: any)",d="Replaces one constant in a Lua function or stack level by one-based index. Invalid stack levels raise \"Level out of range\", non-Lua functions raise \"Lua function expected\", indexes below 1 raise \"Constant index starts at 1\", and indexes past the available constants raise \"Constant index out of range"},{n="setstack",c="Debug",s="setstack(level: number, index: number, value: any)",d="Replaces one stack slot value in a Lua stack frame. level and index are required numbers. level must satisfy 0 <= level < the current call stack depth; invalid levels raise \"Level out of range\". C closure frames raise \"Lua function expected\". index is one-based and must refer to an existing stack sl"},{n="setupvalue",c="Debug",s="setupvalue(target: function | number, index: number, value: any)",d="Replaces one upvalue in a Lua function or stack level by one-based index. Invalid stack levels raise \"Level out of range\", non-Lua functions raise \"Lua function expected\", indexes below 1 raise \"Upvalue index starts at 1\", and indexes past the available upvalues raise \"Upvalue index is out of range\""},{n="filtergc",c="Environment",s="filtergc(filterType: string, options: table, returnOne?: boolean): table | function | nil",d="Searches live garbage-collected tables or functions that match the supplied filters. filterType must be \"table\" or \"function\". options must be a table. It returns result (table | function | nil). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil results and recoverable errors."},{n="getgc",c="Environment",s="getgc(includeTables?: boolean): table",d="Returns an array table of live Luau garbage-collected objects visible to the API. Functions and userdata-like objects are included by default. Tables are included only when includeTables is true. get_gc_objects is an alias. It returns objects (table). Use the returns table to separate successful val"},{n="getgenv",c="Environment",s="getgenv(): table",d="Returns the current executor environment table by pushing LUA_ENVIRONINDEX. The function takes no arguments, returns exactly one value, and has no registered alias. Repository call-sites use the returned table to read and write shared executor globals such as __siApiCache and saveinstance."},{n="getrenv",c="Environment",s="getrenv(): table",d="Returns the Roblox global environment table. The function takes no arguments and returns exactly one value. It returns environment (table). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil results and recoverable errors. ### 📌 Example Read the Roblox global environment table returned by "},{n="getscriptglobals",c="Environment",s="getscriptglobals(): table",d="Returns a new table containing the current LUA_GLOBALSINDEX values for _G and shared. The function takes no arguments, creates a fresh table, assigns _G from LUA_GLOBALSINDEX._G and shared from LUA_GLOBALSINDEX.shared, and returns exactly one value. It does not return the full global table, and no a"},{n="gettenv",c="Environment",s="gettenv(thread: thread): table",d="Returns the environment table stored on a Luau thread. getstateenv is an alias. It returns environment (table). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil results and recoverable errors. ### 📌 Example Read the environment table stored on a Luau thread."},{n="setclipboard",c="Environment",s="setclipboard(text: any)",d="Writes one value to the Windows system clipboard as text. The value is converted to a string. The function returns no status value, whether the clipboard write succeeds or fails. toclipboard is an alias. It does not return data. Treat the call as an action and handle errors around the call site when"},{n="setrbxclipboard",c="Environment",s="setrbxclipboard(text: string)",d="Writes a required string to the Windows clipboard using Roblox Studio clipboard data format. The function returns no status value, whether the clipboard write succeeds or fails. It does not return data. Treat the call as an action and handle errors around the call site when needed."},{n="getmetafield",c="Metatables",s="getmetafield(target: any, field: string): any | nil",d="Returns a raw metafield value from the target metatable. target may be any value, and field must be a string. The function does not call the metafield, does not invoke __index lookup, and returns nil when the metatable or field is missing. It returns fieldValue (any | nil). Use the returns table to "},{n="getnamecallmethod",c="Metatables",s="getnamecallmethod(): string | nil",d="Returns the current namecall method string when one is available, otherwise nil. The function takes no arguments and does not compute a method name from a target object. get_namecall_method is an alias. It returns method (string | nil). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil re"},{n="getrawmetatable",c="Metatables",s="getrawmetatable(target: any): table | nil",d="Returns the metatable currently attached to a target value, or nil when none is present. The function returns exactly one value and does not change the target. debug.getmethods is an alias for getrawmethods. It returns metatable (table | nil). Use the returns table to separate successful values from"},{n="hasmetafield",c="Metatables",s="hasmetafield(target: any, field: string): boolean",d="Returns whether the target value has a non-nil raw metafield with the requested name. The function does not call the metafield, does not invoke __index lookup, and does not change readonly state. It returns hasField (boolean). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil results and "},{n="hasmetatable",c="Metatables",s="hasmetatable(target: any): boolean",d="Returns whether the target value has a metatable. The function returns one boolean and does not return or change the metatable itself. It returns hasMetatable (boolean). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil results and recoverable errors."},{n="isreadonly",c="Metatables",s="isreadonly(target: table): boolean",d="Returns whether a table is readonly. The argument must be a table, and the function does not change it. It returns readOnly (boolean). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil results and recoverable errors. ### 📌 Example Read the readonly flag stored on a table."},{n="makereadonly",c="Metatables",s="makereadonly(target: table)",d="Marks a table as readonly and returns no values. It does not return data. Treat the call as an action and handle errors around the call site when needed. ### 📌 Example Set a table's readonly flag to true."},{n="makewriteable",c="Metatables",s="makewriteable(target: table)",d="Marks a table as writable and returns no values. It does not return data. Treat the call as an action and handle errors around the call site when needed. ### 📌 Example Set a table's readonly flag to false."},{n="setnamecallmethod",c="Metatables",s="setnamecallmethod(method: string)",d="Replaces the current namecall method string when a current namecall method exists. The method argument must be a string. If no current namecall method exists, the call returns no values and does not create one. set_namecall_method is an alias. It does not return data. Treat the call as an action and"},{n="setrawmetatable",c="Metatables",s="setrawmetatable(target: any, metatable: table | nil): any",d="Sets the metatable for a target value and returns the original target. metatable must be a table or nil; nil clears the metatable. debug.setmethods is an alias for setrawmethods. It returns target (any). Use the returns table to separate successful values from nil results and recoverable errors."},{n="setreadonly",c="Metatables",s="setreadonly(target: table, readonly: boolean)",d="Sets whether a table is readonly and returns no values. It does not return data. Treat the call a