rors return an error string; completed requests return a response table."},{n="setfflag",c="Miscellaneous",s="setfflag(name: string, value: any): boolean",d="Sets a Roblox fast flag by exact name. Accepted value types depend on the detected flag type. The function returns true after a supported write and false when the flag is missing, unsupported, or the value is not accepted. It returns updated (boolean). Use the returns table to separate successful va"},{n="setfpscap",c="Miscellaneous",s="setfpscap(value: number)",d="Sets the FPS cap value and returns no values. Values that are non-finite, less than or equal to 0, or greater than 2000 are treated as 2000. It does not return data. Treat the call as an action and handle errors around the call site when needed. ### 📌 Example Set the TaskScheduler FPS cap field and "}}

